< The measures are scored against the construction label on a selection task. An anchor and nine candidate regions are drawn; each measure ranks the candidates by their distance to the anchor and retains the $k$ closest, where $k$ is the number of true matches. Giving every measure the same $k$ removes threshold choice from the comparison entirely; supplying $k$ is itself an oracle, and the application chooses no $k$ but reads the ordering with the clinical calibration (Section~\ref{sec:application}). Performance is summarized by the AUC for discriminating true matches from discordant candidates (chance = 0.5) and by the probability that the $k$ retained regions include at least one discordant region. The task ran 10{,}000 replications per cell at the base grid ($n = 25$--100 per region) and 3{,}000 at the extended grid ($n = 150$--2{,}000). The extension to $n = 2{,}000$ is what makes the classification below possible. The extended grid, the accuracy target and the definitions of the two behaviours below were fixed after the base-grid results had been seen, and the Monte Carlo intervals of Table~\ref{tab:study2_required_n_mc} were added later; the reported target is the middle of the three examined.
