< \begin{enumerate}[1.]
< \item Bias: Small relative to each scenario's $W_1$ at $n \geq 100$ for S3--S7, with positive bias largest near the boundary (S1, where the true value is zero: \numval{biasS1n100} at $n = 100$) and negligible for the larger-shift scenarios (S3: \numval{biasS3n100}, S4: $-\numval{biasS4n100abs}$ at $n = 100$).
