< The principal contribution of this paper is a distributional similarity measure for effect modifiers whose heterogeneity bound is attained and whose calibration constant is a per-unit clinical slope. The $W_1$ distance, combined with bootstrap confidence intervals and clinical calibration via $\Delta_{\max}$ or $L^*$, supplies a reproducible quantitative basis for the judgment of ``similar enough'', operationalizing the similarity of effect modifier distributions that ICH E17 describes, and informing, not prescribing, pooling decisions.
